From e376e60df24c815201cddf25b4b897cedd3befc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:05:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(binary): classify the vendor's JDK and Native Image Kit
 runtimes

Add the java-binary-vendor-jdk and java-binary-vendor-nik classifiers. A
vendor runtime is identified from its JVM library (libjvm.so,
libjvm.dylib or jvm.dll): the java.vm.vendor constant (jvmvendor.Vendor)
and the HotSpot banner "... JRE (21.0.2+14-LTS), built on ..." give vendor
and version; the release file's IMPLEMENTOR, when present, must agree. A
runtime with GraalVM markers (GRAALVM_VERSION in release, lib/svm/,
bin/native-image) is the vendor's Native Image Kit, versioned from its
java.vendor.version (Liberica-NIK-23.1.0-1 -> 23.1.0+1). Packages are
pkg:generic/bellsoft/liberica-jdk and pkg:generic/bellsoft/liberica-nik
without a CPE: the NVD dictionary has no entry for them, and the generic
oracle:openjdk CPE made every CVE show up twice.

One runtime, one package: the generic java-binary classes and the JVM
release cataloger leave the vendor's runtimes to these classifiers. Other
vendors are classified as before.
